CGOA Streaming: Expose a C streaming API as a Go channel interface

Given a C streaming API:

typedef void(*chunk_cb)(const uint8_t* data, size_t len, void* user);
void start_stream(const char* source, chunk_cb cb, void* user);
void stop_stream(void* context);

The callback may run on any thread, and buffers are for one-shot use. Implement a CGOA wrapper exposing:

func StartStream(source string) (<-chan []byte, func(), error)

- The wrapper must copy chunks into Go memory, not expose C pointers to Go, manage lifetimes with a cgo.Handle, support cancel/cleanup, and allow two streams to run in parallel with different sources. Provide the C header/stub, a minimal C implementation, the Go binding, and a short Go program showing two concurrent streams?

questions.explanation:
## Why This Is Asked

This question probes CGO callbacks from C to Go, cross-thread safe streaming, memory management between C and Go, and robust cancellation/backpressure handling in real-time data flows.

## Key Concepts

- CGO callback lifetimes across Go and C threads
- Memory management for C strings vs Go strings
- Per-stream state with context cancellation and resource cleanup
- Backpressure coordination between producers (C) and consumers (Go)

## Code Example

